00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.445
always seen as the new media person.

00:08:23.445 --> 00:08:27.310
- And this was post April 2000
where things melted, right?

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.360
- Yeah, so, that's right.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.210
- And you saw it as the opportunity.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.190
- I saw it as an opportunity.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.860
I mean most people thought
it was a terrible time.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.720
My view is that there's never a good time,

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.067
there's no time when
you're starting a business

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:38.210
and you look around and say, wow,

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.610
this is an awesome time, it's always hard.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.870
But it was the time when I was ready.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.956
And I was done working for other people.

00:08:45.956 --> 00:08:49.250
And so we started what has become ZMC.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.170
And we had just, it's always
fun to tell these stories.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.890
So, we had no offices, no capital,

